Z||000006||My7Fieros||04-21-2001||10:22 PM||||OMG I cant believe how many people actually <I>like</I> having a luggage rack on a Fiero! UUUUGGHHH!!! Most def gotta get a spoiler. <BR>As far as options go, both were....Ive only seen one fastback w/a luggage rack on it...somebody on here w/ a gold one (sorry cant remember who). No offense, really, but Im glad its the only one Ive seen......   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> Luggage racks are for 70's station wagons.<P>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 04-21-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 04-21-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000007||stimpy||04-22-2001||12:15 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=258191&a=1921599&p=16712376&Sequence=0"> <BR>No offense taken. I didn't order it this way. It is a used car, after all. My preference would be a smoothie deck though. I'm not a fan of the wing on fastbacks, tend to make the car look stubby and ruins rear vision. But to each their own.   I do like the look of the wing on 86 & 87 SE's though.||||reg||1
Z||000008||qwikgta||04-22-2001||12:36 AM||||I have never had a Fiero with the rack, but has anyone every really used it.  I would be afraid to put something heavy on it.  Anyone got any pics of crap on your rack.  Maybe we should start a thread with that as a title.<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe<BR>http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||1
Z||000009||Tryxalon||04-22-2001||10:59 AM||||everyone has their personal favorites. <P>Personally, <B> I </B> think the fastbacks look "unfinished" or designed by the unimaginative -- that opinion is shared by few. <P>And I climbed up there and jumped around some. I weigh 250 ... didn't bow, break, or even chip paint.  It is for the "occasional carry of large items" not daily use, and We must admit, the outside mirrors are TOO SMALL! <BR><P>------------------<BR>A Phero Pholly   <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/tryxalon/phollymini.gif">   an obsession.||||reg||1
Z||000010||WKDFIRO||04-22-2001||01:38 PM||||My wife and I used the rack when she wanted to take her 84 with her up to Portland where she was going to school. It worked out well, but just don't pull to hard when tightening down restraining lines. It scared me how easily at least one of the luggage bars popped out! <P>So Cal to Portland in a loaded down Fiero...no thank you!||||reg||12
Z||000011||Cozmo||04-22-2001||05:17 PM||||When I got my GT the salesman (it was an auction car) said, "$150 less without the wing.". He claimed he had a Taurus SVO that he was going to install it on.  I figured this was BS, just a way to get mo' money so I said "Keep the wing.". Sure enough I later found out he DID have a Taurus SVO and DAMN if that Fiero wing didn't look perfect on it...fit like it was made for it. So the GT now has nothing (gonna fill in the holes where the wing was).<BR>On the targa the luggage rack is the only place to carry the roof panel, it's too big to fit anywhere else. Looks kind of stupid there, I was thinking of mounting some big stanchions on the deck lid and putting the roof panel on them. Kinda like a HUGE wing... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">Uncle Ben <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>------------------<BR><B>C02M0</B><BR><I>Suncoast Fieros</I><BR>'85 silver 2M6 4spd. Targa <B>"Silver Streak"</B><BR>'86 black auto GT <B>"Blackbird"</B><BR>'87 white auto Coupe <B>"The Duke"</B>||||reg||2
