Z||000013||tgowens||04-23-2001||01:22 AM||||as far as I know, they were both options for the GT. There were different "packages" offered and the car could be purchased either way. I have the window sticker for one of my GTs and it shows the wing as an option.||||reg||1
Z||000014||BC-GT||04-23-2001||02:25 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/p61a8e0f6833d9c68edd5bbdcc213dda1/fe9b00b5.jpg.orig.jpg"> <P>V53   Luggage Carrier, delete (1984)<BR>V56   Luggage carrier, deck lid (87-88)<BR>V58   Luggage carrier, deck lid (84-86)<BR>D80   Extension, rear end panel (spoiler)<P>Both of them were options. I have the luggage rack on my 85 GT and have highlighted the code in the picture of my option codes. I believe back when these cars were being made that the spoilers were somewhat rare and very desirable but now most new cars have them and fancy wheel rims as well.<P><P>------------------<BR>Darryl Martin<BR>1985 GT <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/pf251a969c96964ef15691e97e7ac4489/feb64e3a.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||MontanaFiero||04-23-2001||03:39 AM||||I was going to say that the luggage rack looks absolutely stupid, then I saw Stimpy's car. It actually looks kinda cool on a fastback. But only on a fastback. I must say, however, that if <I>any</I> car out there needs a <I>functional</I> luggage rack, it's gotta be the Fiero.<P>I would replace the notchback luggage rack with a wing spoiler any day.<P>Just my opinion...<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/blee291/fiero/mtfieroplate.jpg"> ||||reg||1
